# The counter at the shell's priority (roadmap l4.md L2): it never waits, so
# only the time slices let the shell in; the shell still answers. The shell
# is the shell in C, a process among init's (os-server.md P12); DOSBox-X's
# starts in /.
program: shell
define: TEST_COUNTER_SAME
define: TEST_THREAD_REPORT
keys: echo one\necho two\n
---
rx286, test build
@bochs /a$ echo one
@mame /a$ echo one
@dosbox-x /$ echo one
one
@bochs /a$ echo two
@mame /a$ echo two
@dosbox-x /$ echo two
two
@bochs /a$
@mame /a$
@dosbox-x /$
rx286: thread root ran
rx286: thread printer ran
rx286: thread mouse ran
rx286: thread console ran
rx286: thread kbd ran
rx286: thread fd ran
rx286: thread hd ran
rx286: thread serial ran
rx286: thread sound ran
rx286: thread rtc ran
rx286: thread counter ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread thread ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread os ran
rx286: thread thread ran
rx286: thread os ran
